  "generated_text": "1. **Rewrite the equation in standard form:**\n   \\[\n   56x^2 + 27 = 89x - 8\n   \\]\n   Move all terms to one side:\n   \\[\n   56x^2 - 89x + 35 = 0\n   \\]\n\n2. **Factor the quadratic equation:**\n   We know $x = \\frac{5}{7}$ is a solution. Using the factor theorem, we can factor the quadratic equation:\n   \\[\n   56x^2 - 89x + 35 = (7x - 5)(8x - 7)\n   \\]\n\n3. **Solve for the other root:**\n   Set each factor equal to zero:\n   \\[\n   7x - 5 = 0 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad 8x - 7 = 0\n   \\]\n   Solving these gives:\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{5}{7} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x = \\frac{7}{8}\n   \\]\n\nConclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{7}{8}}\n\\]",
  "grade": {
